# Datasets

This folder contains the processed bivariate cause-effect pairs used in the
experiments, together with their regime metadata.

## Contents

- custom_pairs/
  Bivariate datasets used by the app. Each file holds two numeric columns
  (the variable pair). Files prefixed with "capped_400_" are sample-capped
  variants (up to 400 rows per regime) used for the fair-comparison
  experiments with LLMs.

- pairmeta_with_ground_truth.txt
  Regime and ground-truth metadata for every pair. Each row specifies the
  dataset identifier, the cause/effect column indices, a dataset weight, the
  threshold variable, the threshold value, and the ground-truth causal
  direction in the low and high regime.
  Direction codes: 1 means X->Y (cause->effect), -1 means Y->X.
  The low regime contains observations at or below the threshold; the high
  regime contains observations above it.

- datasets.py
  Loading helpers used by the application.

## Documentation

Detailed descriptions of each dataset, including the data sources, the domain
literature used to fix the regime thresholds, and the ground-truth causal
directions within each regime, are provided in the technical supplement
(technical_supplement.tex), in the section "Dataset Descriptions".